    ],
    "notes": "in-range muxed account ids (uint64, 0 to 2^64-1). accepted cases carry the M address and MuxedAccount XDR for key 0x3a..3a with that id, given as JSON numbers above 2^53-1. this bound is not a network rule but a JSON interoperability limit: RFC 8259 section 6 says integers outside [-(2^53)+1, 2^53-1] are not interoperable because implementations commonly hold numbers as IEEE-754 doubles. js-stellar-sdk#1785 is that failure: a number above 2^53-1 lost precision and the operation encoded a different id. each case expects either the exact written id or a refusal (unsafe-integer); encoding any other id fails.",
